1. BIGGEST GAP: the two fast presets do not forge a hello-world commission.
   - Cerebras (`gpt-oss-120b`) sends the finish call as plain assistant content, e.g. `{ "cmd": "python3 -m unittest", "summary": "..." }`, with no tool call. `proof::extract_cmd` finds nothing, every heat ends "no CMD", and the ingot cracks. Make the agent recover a finish (or any declared tool call) that a model emits as JSON content instead of a tool call, robustly and without false positives on ordinary prose or code blocks.
   - Groq (`openai/gpt-oss-20b`) sends a `grep` tool call without its required `pattern`; Groq returns HTTP 400 "Tool call validation failed"; slag treats the 400 as fatal and the founder dies. A provider-side tool-validation 400 must go back to the model as a tool error so it can retry, not abort the run.
