Each role uses its selected provider's default unless you set a model:

| Role | Used for | Env var | `config.toml` key | Flag |
|------|----------|---------|-------------------|------|
| work | Grade 1-2 ingots | `SLAG_MODEL_BASE` | `model_base` | `--model` |
| plan | Grade 3+ ingots, surveyor, founder | `SLAG_MODEL_PLAN` | `model_plan` | `--plan-model` |
| duel | Cast B in a twin-cast duel | `SLAG_MODEL_ALT` | `model_alt` | |
| judge | Assays duel casts | `SLAG_MODEL_JUDGE` | `model_judge` | `--judge-model` |

Model precedence is flag, then environment, then file, then the provider default. Use lowercase keys in the file and uppercase names in the environment.

Use `provider::model` to select another provider for one role. The `::` separator preserves existing OpenRouter IDs, including `openai/gpt-5`.

```bash
slag --provider cerebras --plan-model openai::gpt-4.1-mini "Build a Slack bot"
```

```toml
provider = "cerebras"
model_base = "gpt-oss-120b"
model_plan = "openai::gpt-4.1-mini"
model_judge = "openrouter::openai/gpt-5"
```

Set a key for each provider you name. A bare model ID uses the selected provider. With OpenRouter selected, `openai/gpt-5` still names an OpenRouter model.

With another provider selected, bare `openrouter/auto` uses that provider's default. Use `openrouter::openrouter/auto` to request OpenRouter routing.

Provider settings join the existing model, duel, screenshot, MCP, and spend settings in the same file. OpenRouter keeps its routing, `reasoning_details` replay, pricing lookup, and attribution headers. slag preserves native DeepSeek `reasoning_content` and Gemini tool signatures across tool calls. Other providers receive supported reasoning fields or omit them.

### MCP servers

An `[mcp]` table adds Model Context Protocol servers over stdio, one command per line:

```toml
[mcp]
README.md:44:slag --provider ollama --model qwen3:8b "Build a local notes app"
README.md:55:| [groq](https://console.groq.com/docs/overview) | `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1` | `GROQ_API_KEY` | `qwen/qwen3.8-27b` |
README.md:56:| [cerebras](https://inference-docs.cerebras.ai/resources/openai) | `https://api.cerebras.ai/v1` | `CEREBRAS_API_KEY` | `qwen-3.8-27b` |
README.md:62:| [ollama](https://docs.ollama.com/api/openai-compatibility) | `http://localhost:11434/v1` | None | `qwen3:8b` |
README.md:82:Override a preset's endpoint with `SLAG_BASE_URL` or `base_url` in the file. Supply the API root, such as `https://example.com/v1`, without `/chat/completions`. `SLAG_OPENROUTER_BASE` overrides OpenRouter only.
README.md:84:For separate endpoints in a mixed run, use `SLAG_<PROVIDER>_BASE_URL` or `<provider>_base_url`. Endpoint precedence is provider environment, generic environment, OpenRouter alias, provider file, generic file, then preset. slag rejects foreign preset hosts before authentication and does not follow HTTP redirects.
README.md:256:| `SLAG_OPENROUTER_BASE` | Legacy OpenRouter-only base URL override |
CLAUDE.md:87:| groq | `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1` | `GROQ_API_KEY` | `qwen/qwen3.8-27b` |
CLAUDE.md:88:| cerebras | `https://api.cerebras.ai/v1` | `CEREBRAS_API_KEY` | `qwen-3.8-27b` |
CLAUDE.md:94:| ollama | `http://localhost:11434/v1` | None | `qwen3:8b` |
CLAUDE.md:100:Override any API root with `SLAG_BASE_URL` or `base_url`. Keep `/chat/completions` off the root. `SLAG_OPENROUTER_BASE` overrides OpenRouter only. Provider-specific overrides use `SLAG_<PROVIDER>_BASE_URL` or `<provider>_base_url`.
CLAUDE.md:102:Endpoint precedence is provider environment, generic environment, legacy alias, provider file, generic file, then preset. Provider-specific overrides let mixed roles use separate proxies. slag rejects foreign preset hosts before authentication and does not follow HTTP redirects.
