engine-20261015_205021.jsonl {'event': 'finish', 'summary': '## 1. OVERVIEW\nWe will create a minimal Python script `hello.py` that prints the string “hello” when executed. Accompanying it will be a unit test module `test_hello.py` that verifies the script’s output using the standard `unittest` framework.\n\n## 2. COMPONENTS\n| Name          | Purpose                                 | Complexity | Dependencies | Skill |\n|---------------|------------------------------------------|------------|--------------|-------|\n| `hello.py`    | CLI script that prints “hello”.          | 1          | None         | cli |\n| `test_hello.py` | Unit test validating printed output.   | 2          | `hello.py`, `unittest` | default |\n\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n```\nproject_root/\n├── hello.py          # prints hello\n└── test_hello.py    # unittest for hello.py\n```\n*`hello.py`* defines a `main()` function that writes “hello” to `stdout`. The script calls `main()` under `if __name__ == "__main__":`.  \n*`test_hello.py`* captures `stdout` via `io.StringIO` and `unittest.mock.patch`, invokes `hello.main()`, and asserts the captured string equals “hello\\n”.\n\nData flow: test → patch `sys.stdout` → call `hello.main()` → output captured → assertion.\n\n## 4. DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n```\n[hello.py] ──▶ [test_hello.py]\n```\n`test_hello.py` depends on the implementation in `hello.py`.\n\n## 5. RISKS\n- **Low complexity**: trivial logic, minimal risk of bugs.  \n- **Integration point**: test must correctly patch `sys.stdout`; mis‑patching could hide failures.  \n- **External dependencies**: only Python standard library; no version‑specific features.\n\n## 6. FORGING SEQUENCE\n1. **Foundation** – scaffold project directory, create empty `hello.py` and `test_hello.py`.  \n2. **Core logic** – implement `main()` in `hello.py` to print “hello”.  \n3. **Integration** – write test harness in `test_hello.py`, import `hello`, patch `stdout`, and assert output.  \n4. **Polish** – add `if __name__ == "__main__":` guard, ensure test runs via `python -m unittest` and passes.\n\n## 7. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- Running `python hello.py` prints exactly `hello` followed by a newline.  \n- Executing `python -m unittest` discovers `test_hello.py` and all tests pass (exit code\u202f0).  \n- No external packages are required; the code works on Python\u202f3.8+.'}
